; PLACEHOLDER values, easy to retune here. Rationale (Phase 15d-ter): keeping a fragment must feel like a real
; power-up, so the DAMAGE of each tier grows (1, 2, 3: a clean 50 / 25 / 17 hits on boss 2) while the cooldown, speed,
; reach and hitbox stay as they were. Sustained damage per second (damage / max(cooldown, startup + recovery)):
; tier 0 = 1.00, tier 1 = 2.22, tier 2 = 2.50. Tier 0 stays well below the sword (2.22 dps); tiers 1 and 2 may match or
; pass the light sword (they are the reward for keeping fragments) but never beat the heavy slash (2.31 dps) or the
; dash slash (2.63 dps) by more than 15%. Wave damage is an integer, so 1 -> 2 is the smallest step above tier 0.

